\begin_layout Section*
AIM:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The primary aim of this project is to design and develop a 32-bit RISC-V
 processor core targeted for ASIC implementation, incorporating essential
 architectural features required for modern embedded and low-power applications.
 The processor will support advanced functionalities such as Memory Protection
 and Management (PMP/MMU), Control and Status Registers (CSRs), Interrupt
 and Exception Handling, and Debug Support compliant with the RISC-V privilege
 and debug specifications.
 The goal is to build a standards-compliant, synthesizable core that can
 be used as a soft IP for academic research or industrial integration into
 SoCs, with a focus on scalability, verification, and ASIC readiness.
\end_layout

